<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunshine Records (Australia) was an Australian independent pop music record label of the mid-1960s, established by Ivan Dayman, Pat Aulton, and Nat Kipner. It was known for its fully integrated pop music company and its biggest act was a solo singer."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IVAN DAYMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ivan Dayman was a promoter who established Sunshine Records (Australia) in late 1964 and was involved in creating a fully integrated pop music company."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAT AULTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pat Aulton was a musician-producer-arranger-songwriter who collaborated with Ivan Dayman and Nat Kipner to establish Sunshine Records (Australia)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAT KIPNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nat Kipner was an entrepreneur, producer, and songwriter who co-founded Sunshine Records (Australia) and later founded Spin Records. He was involved in the early days of Sunshine Records and then sold his share in 1965."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIN RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spin Records was a label founded by Nat Kipner after he left Sunshine Records."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (UNITED STATES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunshine Records (United States) was a small California-based record label of the early 1920s, producing early jazz and blues records. It was actually manufactured by Nordskog Records and issued by Nordskog, with labels pasted over the Nordskog labels."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORDSKOG RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nordskog Records manufactured and issued Sunshine Records (United States) records, with labels pasted over the Nordskog labels."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIKES BROS. PHONOGRAPH CO. INC.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spikes Bros. Phonograph Co. Inc. was mentioned as the manufacturer of Sunshine Records (United States) labels, though they were actually manufactured by Nordskog Records."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTO RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arto Records is believed to have made an error in pressing the labels onto the Sunshine Records (United States) records."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICK SPRINGFIELD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rick Springfield is mentioned as the future star whose recording debut was produced by Ian 'Molly' Meldrum for 's Bikie Boys'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IAN 'MOLLY' MELDRUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ian 'Molly' Meldrum produced the recording debut of Rick Springfield for 's Bikie Boys'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSSIE BYRNE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ossie Byrne collaborated with Nat Kipner on the short-lived Downunder Records during mid-1966."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE BEE GEES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Bee Gees were managed by Nat Kipner briefly during mid-1966."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FESTIVAL'S LEEDON LABEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Festival's Leedon label released The Bee Gees from their contract after Nat Kipner persuaded them to do so."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN SPIKES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"John Spikes is part of the Spikes Bros. Phonograph Co. Inc., mentioned in relation to the manufacturing of Sunshine Records (United States) labels."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTO RECORDS ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arto Records made an error in pressing the labels onto the Sunshine Records (United States) records."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORDSKOG MANUFACTURING ERROR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nordskog Records made an error in manufacturing the labels for Sunshine Records (United States) records, with labels pasted over the Nordskog labels."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA) ENTERPRISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunshine Records (Australia) was known for its fully integrated pop music company that included artist management, bookings, record production, record labels, venue management, and concert promotion."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (UNITED STATES) RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunshine Records (United States) produced early jazz and blues records in the early 1920s."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA)&quot;" target="&quot;IVAN DAYMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Ivan Dayman established Sunshine Records (Australia) and was involved in creating a fully integrated pop music company."</data>
      <data key="d5">"establishment, leadership"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA)&quot;" target="&quot;PAT AULTON&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Pat Aulton collaborated with Ivan Dayman and Nat Kipner to establish Sunshine Records (Australia)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"collaboration, establishment"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA)&quot;" target="&quot;NAT KIPNER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Nat Kipner co-founded Sunshine Records (Australia) and later sold his share in 1965."</data>
      <data key="d5">"co-founding, departure"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (AUSTRALIA)&quot;" target="&quot;SPIN RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Nat Kipner founded Spin Records after leaving Sunshine Records."</data>
      <data key="d5">"succession, entrepreneurship"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUNSHINE RECORDS (UNITED STATES)&quot;" target="&quot;NORDSKOG RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sunshine Records (United States) records were actually manufactured by Nordskog Records and issued by Nordskog, with labels pasted over the Nordskog labels."</data>
      <data key="d5">"manufacturing, issuance"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
